  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the required files:\n\n1. **`lib/ansible/galaxy/collection/__init__.py`** \u2014 contains `_extract_tar_dir()` and the tar-extraction driver that builds `collection_tar._ansible_normalized_cache`, a dict keyed by `m.name.removesuffix(os.path.sep)` for every tar member (the custom cache described in the bug report), used instead of `tar.getmember()`/standard lookup, as a workaround comment-referenced to a CPython tarfile bug (bpo-47231).\n2. **`test/units/cli/galaxy/test_collection_extract_tar.py`** \u2014 existing unit tests targeting exactly this extraction path (directory member handling in collection tarballs), the natural home/pattern for the regression test.\n3. **`lib/ansible/galaxy/collection/concrete_artifact_manager.py`** \u2014 companion module using `collection_tar.getmember(MANIFEST_FILENAME)` (the standard-library API contrasted with the custom cache), relevant context for the \"workaround no longer necessary\" claim.\n4. **`changelogs/fragments/a-g-col-install-directory-with-trailing-sep.yml`** \u2014 the changelog fragment documenting the original trailing-separator fix this cache was built to support, confirming intent/history.",
